Negative compile tests of gucefMATH

Each translation unit in this directory is expected NOT to compile. They are not part of any build.
A test passes when the compiler rejects the file and its error output names the identifier that the
file states in the comment "the compiler error must name ...".

Procedure for one file, with the include directories of the module build (adapt the compiler as needed):

  g++ -fsyntax-only \
      -I../../../common/include -I../../../platform/gucefMATH/include \
      -I../../../platform/gucefCORE/include -I../../../platform/gucefCORE/include/c_api \
      -I../../../platform/gucefCORE/include/linux -I../../../platform/gucefMT/include \
      static_assert_false.cpp 2>&1 | grep GucefMathExpectedStaticAssertFailure

Pass: g++ exits with an error AND grep prints a line. Fail: g++ succeeds, or the error does not name the identifier.
Run it with -std=c++98 and with the default standard: both forms of GUCEF_MATH_STATIC_ASSERT must name it.
